<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Pricing</span>
<h1>Honda Wave Short vs Long-Term Rental Cost in Hanoi: Cost Planning Guide</h1>
<p>The Honda Wave carries three verified prices in Hanoi: 150,000 VND per day, 700,000 VND per week, and 900,000 to 1,200,000 VND per month. The choice between short and long-term renting is not about preference; it is arithmetic. This guide puts the three rates side by side, finds the break-even points, and shows which structure fits which stay.</p>
<p>We cover the three verified rates as one ladder, the per-day cost of each rung, the break-even points where the structure switches, budgeting a short stay against a long one, the practical differences beyond price, and the questions that settle the decision at the counter. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> hub, see the full model range at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, and check common questions on the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The three-rate ladder</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">Per-day cost of each structure</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">The break-even points</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">Budgeting a short stay</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-5">Budgeting a long stay</a></li>
